# BMS Molecular Translation — winning component: rigel_mu image->InChI model

This directory contains the code for the primary model used in the final submission:
a ConvNeXt-Tiny encoder + 6-layer transformer decoder trained from scratch on the
competition training set to map a molecular image to its InChI string.

## Files
- `model.py`      — encoder/decoder with preallocated-KV-cache greedy decoding (`generate_fast`).
- `prep.py`       — builds BPE tokenizer targets and the 20k holdout split from `data/train_labels.csv`.
- `train.py`      — training loop (bf16, AdamW, cosine, label smoothing) with holdout Levenshtein eval.
- `infer.py`      — inference (batched, `--fast`, incremental flush) -> `image_id,InChI`.
- `run_final_infer.sh` — final holdout (20k) + all-test (484,838) inference.

## Reproduce
```
pyenv shell sis-black
# 1) labels/tokenizer + split (CPU)
python prep.py
# 2) train (single A100): ~30k steps, batch 128, img 384, ~7h
python train.py --enc convnext_tiny.fb_in22k_ft_in1k --out_index 2 --img_size 384 \
  --batch 128 --d_model 512 --nhead 8 --layers 6 --dim_ff 2048 --lr 3e-4 \
  --enc_lr_mult 0.3 --epochs 3.0 --eval_every 1000 --eval_n 1024 --tag v1
# 3) inference
python infer.py --ckpt ck_v1_last.pt --ids holdout_20k.csv --imgroot ../../data/train \
  --out rigel_val20k.csv --bs 384 --fast 1
python infer.py --ckpt ck_v1_last.pt --ids test_all_ordered.csv --imgroot ../../data/test \
  --out rigel_test_all.csv --bs 384 --fast 1
```
Final holdout mean Levenshtein = **8.58** (20k, median 0, exact 50.4%).

